{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790964168,"nonce":"t5kjZliQlFQQNSQplqWpshbBCNQ=","title":"Components: @:state fields and reading signals without .get()","message":"The spec's component shape is\n\n    class CounterView extends View {\n        @:state var count:Int = 0;\n        function render() '\u003cvbox rounded={count * 2}\u003e\u003ctext\u003eValue: ${count}\u003c/text\u003e\u003c/vbox\u003e';\n    }\n\nhxx (closed 5088856) needs signals read explicitly: rounded={count.get() * 2}. To reach the spec's form:\n- a build macro turning each @:state field into a Signal-backed property (count reads Signal.get, count = x sets it), so templates and code read plain values;\n- hxx then treats an attribute expression that reads a @:state field as reactive, as it does .get() calls today;\n- render() as a template-bodied function, wired to Owner so a component's computeds and nodes go with it.\nComponents extend or wrap Div (the stated convention), so View is likely Div plus this macro.","files":null}]}